gay or bisexual female protagonists is favoured but not a deal breaker)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bRick Riordan's books are VERY Scion-like. Any of his stories will work, just make sure you're starting at the beginning of one of his chronicles. He's got a lot of story arcs, so make sure you're not buying the third book of a chronicle or something.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf you're looking for gay representation, he's incorporated several gay characters into his stories thus far. In one of his most recent series, he just introduced a gender fluid transgendered character named Alex Fiero, and she's AWESOME. Seriously. Best character in the series. For that one, look for the &quot;Magnus Chase and the Gods of Asgard&quot; series. The third and final book is coming out next month, I believe.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo yeah, you can't go wrong with anything by Riordan.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf you're into comic books, Wonder Woman is very Scion-like. A new run has just started this week by James Robinson, and it's off to an interesting start. Pressure has been mounting to reveal Wonder Woman to be bisexual, as well. It's just a matter of time before someone pulls that trigger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T05:34:23-07:00","id":1144717,"title":"","content":"the rick riordan's books look good, although something a little less young adult would be better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T07:00:53-07:00","id":1144748,"title":"","content":"That's the trick, isn't it? I can barely think of anything not YA that actually features the hallmarks of Scion besides American Gods. Vampires and wolves I guess are easier to hook into modern settings or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T07:16:12-07:00","id":1144751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1144686-scion-like-fiction?p=1144711#post1144711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> \u200bIf you're into comic books, Wonder Woman is very Scion-like. A new run has just started this week by James Robinson, and it's off to an interesting start. Pressure has been mounting to reveal Wonder Woman to be bisexual, as well. It's just a matter of time before someone pulls that trigger.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A society consisting exclusively of immortal women who severed all contact with <i>man's world</i> for thousands of years before one crashed a plane on their island?<br /> <br /> Yeah, can't see how there wouldn't be a large number of gays and bisexuals on Themyscira.<br /> <br /> <br /> Last time I heard about WW, though, she had become a goddess of war (the very thing the Amazons stand against), but I don't know if that got rebooted or not.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, I've heard the Percy Jackson series is pretty much Scion, if the Theoi opened up a boot camp for Heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T07:56:59-07:00","id":1144769,"title":"","content":"I can not recommend the Rick Riordan books enough. They are one of my all time favorite books. His first series, Percy Jackson and the Olympians, definitely skews more towards the Young end of the Young Adult demographic, but he hits a decently mature tone by the fifth and final book in that series and it carries through all his later books. And while the original series had a cast of mostly white straight cisgender individuals, the later books have much more diverse casts. Heck, the Trials of Apollo series have several queer characters, including acknowledging that Apollo himself was bisexual in the myths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9296-zeldafan42","name":"Zeldafan42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9296_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T08:06:47-07:00","id":1144773,"title":"","content":"thanks peeps, tbh I'm just looking for something (not YA) Urban fantasy that isnt vamps, werewolves and some sort of mage analogue, cos honestly im a bit tired of it (i mean not completely but i could do with some variety) i hate to blame world of darkness but i do, I'll give the Percy Jackson books a go (the film was bad - but i have heard it is a bit hated by the fandom).<br /> If i want to avoid the younger young adult bits where should i start?<br /> <br /> any other suggestions welcome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12845,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","user":"ahather","date":".  something i forgot to add 09-28-2017, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T08:59:28-07:00","id":1144798,"title":"","content":"Some suggestions for adult fiction with a divine theme: The Immortals by Jordanna Brodsky \u2013 Artemis as a detective in modern New York; Gods Behaving Badly by Marie Phillips - comedic novel about the Greek gods in the modern day; Dark Descendant series by Jenna Black, reincarnated deities, urban fantasy with romance overtones; the comic series the Wicked &amp; the Divine cannot be recommended highly enough; James Lovegrove's several &quot;Godpunk&quot; novels are popular, though I don't like them myself. Hopefully that gives you some ideas!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https